This source package is built from the upstream release asset
0c-ime-<version>.tar.xz (not the "Source code" archive generated by GitHub).
That asset includes assets/data/ with the compiled dictionary and
models/pairing.lock.json; a plain Git checkout does not, so run
"make assets MODELS=0" before testing a build from Git.

The 0c-settings Tauri application is not built by this package yet.  Its
Rust/Tauri dependency stack is not packaged in Debian, and it is not needed
for the engine or the Fcitx5/IBus shells.  Add it as another binary package
once those dependencies are available.

Go 1.26 or newer is required by go.mod.  The build is driven through the
upstream Makefile (SETTINGS=0), so the dh-golang addon is not used.  If the
versions of the packaged Go modules differ from go.sum, adapt the build with
the Debian Go team's usual module patches (or lower the Go directive
upstream if the code builds with an older toolchain).

Tests are disabled by default: the upstream go test suite needs the module
cache and the dictionary in assets/data.  Enable override_dh_auto_test once
the module dependencies are pinned for Debian.

The neural models are non-free (MIT weights, but no training source) and are
packaged separately as 0c-ime-models in the non-free archive.  They install
to /usr/share/0c/neural/{select,punct} and are detected as bundled models.
debian/control will gain "Suggests: 0c-ime-models" once that package is in
the archive.

Before the first upload, add the ITP bug number to debian/changelog and fill
in Vcs-Git/Vcs-Browser after creating the packaging repository.
